<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><h1 class="st-title">Da Tianxing</h1><p class="st-meta">928 CE – 929 CE · capital Yangjumie</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A one-year dynasty in Yunnan under Zhao Shanzheng, a figurehead raised to the throne at Yangjumie after the fall of Da Changhe.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 928 the powerful official <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-ganzhen">Yang Ganzhen</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zheng-longdan">Zheng Longdan</a>, last ruler of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/da-changhe">Da Changhe</a>, and placed the minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-shanzheng">Zhao Shanzheng</a> on the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangjumie">Yangjumie</a> as ruler of Da Tianxing.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Almost nothing is known of the regime beyond its existence; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-shanzheng">Zhao Shanzheng</a> appears to have been a puppet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-ganzhen">Yang Ganzhen</a> and the great families of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-erhai">Erhai</a> region, who continued the institutions inherited from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nanzhao">Nanzhao</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 929 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-ganzhen">Yang Ganzhen</a> removed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhao-shanzheng">Zhao Shanzheng</a> and took the throne himself, founding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/da-yining">Da Yining</a>. The rapid succession of dynasties ended only with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dali-kingdom">Dali Kingdom</a> in 937.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 928 CE – 929 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">China, Tibet and Mongolia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.17%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>928 CE – 929 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yangjumie</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zhao Shanzheng</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bai, Middle Chinese for writing</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/china">China</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Datianxing</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=928&amp;focus=da-tianxing" aria-label="Da Tianxing on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7411 989 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Da Tianxing lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7731 1245h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M7731 1245h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day China. <a href="/atlas?year=928&amp;focus=da-tianxing">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
